    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9db4d1f_93f766be",
        "filename": "bp2build/build_conversion_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 1315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T03:46:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s difficult to trace through this code to understand what exactly is being tested (expected and actual data). It\u0027s totally fine to have some duplication for readability. \n\nPlease split this up into individual test functions with explicit test data (like the other tests in this directory), and avoid relying on complex internal test infrastructure to dynamically construct test data like this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1261,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1315,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "c6f86bb366822f3e652acd4fdfbee34b7074c641",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8fff8db1_52a5a443",
        "filename": "bp2build/build_conversion_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 1315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1887575
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T15:04:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the syntax I\u0027m aiming for with this is:\n```\ncollectivelyTest(commonBazelAttributeMultiplyUsed,\n    collectiveTest{oneSoongProp, itsValue, itsBazelValue},\n    collectiveTest{anotherSoongProp, alsoItsValue, alsoItsBazelValue},\n    ...\n)\n...\nsingularTest(commonBazelAttributeUsedOnce, itsSoongProp, itsValue, itsBazelValue)\n...\n// Run the auto-collected set of all the prop-\u003eattr assignments, with the multiply-used attrs having their values collected into an array for them, and the once-used attrs simply having their own entry\n```\n\nI\u0027m trying to avoid the case where when adding a new property we have to keep 2+ test cases in sync, along different semantics: one mapping individually for the attribute, potentially other mixes, and another collecting all the properties per multiply-used attribute.\n\nIs splitting all that out into replicated tests to keep in sync preferable?",
      "parentUuid": "f9db4d1f_93f766be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1261,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1315,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "c6f86bb366822f3e652acd4fdfbee34b7074c641",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "102a25e9_872e16be",
        "filename": "bp2build/build_conversion_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 1315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1887575
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T15:12:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i.e., data input and output are still paired, so it provides the focused difference between the tests, just without repeated exterior context and without keeping individual, potentially mixed, and all-at-once tests in-sync.",
      "parentUuid": "8fff8db1_52a5a443",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1261,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1315,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "c6f86bb366822f3e652acd4fdfbee34b7074c641",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1271bc89_f6eebdf5",
        "filename": "bp2build/build_conversion_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 31
      },
      "lineNbr": 1315,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T15:22:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general, DRY isn\u0027t what we\u0027re aiming for with tests. https://testing.googleblog.com/2019/12/testing-on-toilet-tests-too-dry-make.html\n\nIt is preferable to minimize logic in tests and it should be quite clear what the inputs/expected outputs are:\nhttps://testing.googleblog.com/2014/07/testing-on-toilet-dont-put-logic-in.html",
      "parentUuid": "8fff8db1_52a5a443",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1261,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1315,
        "endChar": 0
